# Claude AI / Copilot agent internal files.
#
# The agent's SHARED configuration is project infrastructure and must survive a
# clone — instructions, scoped rules, skills and hooks are worth nothing if they
# exist only on the machine that wrote them. Per-developer state (approved
# permissions, session locks, caches) stays local. Note `.claude/*` rather than
# `.claude/`: a file cannot be re-included while its parent directory is itself
# excluded — the same reason the backend/tests block below is written this way.
.claude/*
CLAUDE.md
!.claude/CLAUDE.md
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/rules/
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/hooks/

# Internal docs (not needed to run the project) — `docs/*` rather than `docs/`
# so the one subtree below can be re-included; already-tracked docs are
# unaffected either way.
docs/*
# …except the feature-artifact templates and the policy for using them, which
# the workflow refers to and so must exist on a fresh clone.
!docs/features/

# Demo/test scripts (local only)
seed_demo.py
scope-foodball-demo.xlsx
verify-docker.sh
verify-docker.ps1

# Test & debug scripts (local only — not for repo)
test_*.py
*_test.py
**/test_*.py
**/*_test.py
backend/tests/
tests/
seed_test_users.py

# Exploratory / one-off scripts (local only)
create_dashboard.py
explore_datasets.py
check_*.py
# …but scripts/ci/ holds real gates, not one-offs. preflight.sh and CI call this
# one, so an ignored copy would mean a gate that cannot run on a fresh clone.
!scripts/ci/check_*.py
# Same for the workflow-gate tests: `test_*.py` is ignored globally, and a test
# that vanishes on a fresh clone cannot protect the Stop hook.
!scripts/ci/test_*.py
fix_*.py
add_*.py
run.py
_tmp/
tmp_build_vi_ai_report.py
_quarantine/
scripts/_wb*_bundle.json
scripts/audit_workboard.py
scripts/production_demo_*
scripts/seed_*workboard.sql
scripts/verify_*workboard.py
backend/scripts/audit_dimension_sql.py
backend/scripts/dedupe_view_binding.py

# Local large data / one-off bootstrap helpers
2019-Nov.csv
_create_ds.py
install-docker-and-run.sh
*.xlsx
*.csv

# Release hygiene: local artifacts, sensitive backups, non-runtime references
.artifacts/
.env.bak.*
# (The MCP servers once under Skill-AppBI/ are gone: the two builder servers were
# removed — their venvs/logs sit in .artifacts/removed-mcp/ — and the guardrail
# moved to scripts/guardrail/, which needs no ignore rules of its own.)
dashboard_example/
demo_dataset/
example/
*.workboard.json
UI_LINEAR_AUDIT_CHECKLIST.md
Design System Inspired by Linear.md
ai-chat/AI_CHAT_SYSTEM_DOC.md
ai-chat/UPGRADE_PLAN.md
ai-chat/UPGRADE_PLAN_V2.md
ai-chat/WORKBOARDS_END_TO_END_DESIGN.md
backend/README.md
frontend/README.md
# Serena MCP — machine-specific config (absolute paths/username) + local LSP cache; do not commit.
# `.mcp.example.json` IS committed: it carries only the repo-relative servers
# (the engineering guardrail), so a fresh clone can register them without
# inheriting anyone's absolute paths.
.mcp.json
!.mcp.example.json
.vscode/mcp.json
.serena/
# E2E (Playwright) — local deps, secrets, run artifacts, saved auth session
e2e/node_modules/
e2e/.env
e2e/.auth/
e2e/test-results/
e2e/playwright-report/
e2e/blob-report/
e2e/.cache/
e2e/shots/
e2e/_*.mjs
e2e/_*.png
# …but the Playwright SPECS are project code → track them. The bare `tests/`
# ignore (above) would otherwise drop e2e/tests/ wholesale; re-include the dir
# (a file can't be un-ignored while its parent dir stays excluded) + the specs.
# Local-only helpers (node_modules, .env, .auth, _*.mjs, shots) stay ignored above.
!e2e/tests/
!e2e/tests/**/*.ts
# …but not one-off debugging probes. These dump page text and console errors to
# stdout while chasing a bug; they assert nothing, so committing them would add
# specs to the suite that can never fail. `_helpers.ts` is real shared code, so
# the pattern is `_probe*` rather than `_*`.
e2e/tests/_probe*.ts
!e2e/playwright.config.ts
!e2e/package.json

# ── Local QA / test artifacts (screenshots, debug dumps, harnesses) — never push ──
# Playwright-MCP working dir (page snapshots + screenshots written during testing)
.playwright-mcp/
# Loose root-level test screenshots + API response dumps.
#
# `.artifacts/` (ignored above) is where these belong, and the rules below are
# the safety net for when a tool or a debugging session drops one at the root
# anyway. The convention was declared here once and then not followed — 110
# screenshots and two 300KB+ response dumps accumulated at the repo root, none
# of them tracked but all of them in the way. They now live in
# `.artifacts/screenshots/` and `.artifacts/debug-dumps/`.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.webp
/*.gif
/*.json
!/.mcp.example.json
# Manual-QA output dir: screenshots + HTML fixtures written during browser
# testing. Nothing reads it; it belongs in .artifacts/qa-sessions/.
/test-artifacts/
# Codegraph MCP — local SQLite knowledge-graph cache + generated overview doc (tool artifacts)
.codegraph/
CODEGRAPH.md
# Root-level test run output (Playwright / harness run artifacts)
/test-results/
# Running QA audit doc (working notes, not project code)
EXPLORE_CHART_AUDIT.md
# Chart verification harness (local-only)
scripts/verify-charts/
